# Xcode and Swift, for the VenTrack iOS app.

## The Xcode project itself, because it is GENERATED, not written.
#
# project.rb is the source of truth. It globs VenTrack/**/*.swift and writes
# every build setting, and it mints fresh UUIDs on every run, so a committed
# copy is dirty the moment anyone regenerates and can never be checked for
# staleness in CI. The workflow already regenerates it rather than trusting
# what is committed, which is the correct instinct.
#
# It used to be committed anyway, and that cost real time. The iPad layout
# landed with TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = '1,2' in project.rb and CI compiled it
# green, while the committed project still said '1' and referenced none of the
# new files. Anyone opening it in Xcode therefore built the OLD iPhone only app
# and quite reasonably concluded the iPad layout did not work.
#
# Untracked, `open VenTrack.xcodeproj` fails loudly when you have not run the
# generator, which is a far better failure than silently building last week's
# app. Always:
#
#   cd ios && ruby project.rb && open VenTrack.xcodeproj
#
VenTrack.xcodeproj/

